    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %s</string>
    <string name="about_plugins">All instruments and effects are built in. Android has no system-wide plugin standard like VST on desktop; support for the open AAP format (Audio Plugins for Android) is planned.</string>
    <string name="help_1_title">Channels</string>
    <string name="help_1_text">Each channel is one instrument: a drum, a synth, a sampler or an audio track. Tap its name to pick another sound, add effects or rename it.</string>
    <string name="help_2_title">Patterns</string>
    <string name="help_2_text">A pattern is a short loop. Tap the squares to place drum hits. For melodies open the Notes tab and draw notes on the piano roll.</string>
    <string name="help_3_title">Playlist</string>
    <string name="help_3_text">Lay patterns out on the timeline to build the whole track. PAT plays one pattern in a loop, SONG plays the playlist.</string>
    <string name="help_4_title">Mixer</string>
    <string name="help_4_text">Set the volume and panning of every channel and add effects: reverb, delay, compressor, equalizer and more.</string>
    <string name="help_auto_title">Automation</string>
    <string name="help_auto_text">Make the sound change over time: on the Notes tab open the menu, turn on Automation, pick a knob and draw its curve. The knob follows the curve while the pattern plays.</string>
    <string name="help_5_title">Recording</string>
    <string name="help_5_text">Press ● to record: either notes played on the keys and pads, or your voice from the microphone.</string>
    <string name="help_6_title">Export</string>
    <string name="help_6_text">When the track is ready, open the menu and export it as WAV or M4A. The file appears in the Music/MPS folder.</string>
